# Deep Links

## Route Builders

```typescript
import { deeplink } from "~/shared/lib/deeplinks";

deeplink.toStream(5, "general");           // "/stream/5-general"
deeplink.toTopic(5, "general", "bugs");    // "/stream/5-general/topic/bugs"
deeplink.toMessage(5, "general", "bugs", 12345);  // "…/topic/bugs?msg=12345"
deeplink.toDm(42);                         // "/dm/42"
deeplink.toActivity("starred");            // "/activity/starred"
```

## Shareable URLs

```typescript
const url = deeplink.toShareableUrl("/stream/5-general");
// Web:      "https://app.example.com/stream/5-general"
// Electron: "workspace://open/stream/5-general"
```

## Parsing (incoming deep links)

```typescript
const parsed = deeplink.parse("workspace://open/dm/42");
// { type: "dm", path: "/dm/42", dmId: "42" }

const parsed2 = deeplink.parse("https://app.example.com/stream/5-general/topic/bugs?msg=12345");
// { type: "message", streamSlug: "5-general", topicName: "bugs", messageId: 12345 }
```

## Sharing

```typescript
await deeplink.share({
  title: "#general — bugs",
  url: deeplink.toShareableUrl(deeplink.toTopic(5, "general", "bugs")),
});
// Web Share API → native share dialog (mobile/PWA)
// Fallback → clipboard copy
```

## Electron Custom Protocol

Protocol: `workspace://`

Flow:
1. User clicks `workspace://open/dm/42` in external app
2. OS launches Electron (or focuses existing instance)
3. Main process extracts route from URL
4. Sends `deeplink:navigate` IPC to renderer
5. React navigates to `/dm/42`

Registration: `app.setAsDefaultProtocolClient("workspace")` in main.ts.

## For AI Agent

- Use `deeplink.toStream/toTopic/toDm` to build navigation URLs
- Never construct route strings manually — always use builders
- For "share" buttons: `deeplink.toShareableUrl()` + `deeplink.share()`
- Notification `onClick`: navigate using `deeplink.parse()` result
